that nobody drives against that hay and waggon to-night, Stubberd,” said the corn-merchant.”"},{"id":"mr-grower","name":"Mr. Grower","aliases":["Grower"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s29","summary":"First mention: “My great creditor is Grower, and it is at his hands I shall suffer if at anybody’s; while a fortnight’s forbearance on his part would be enough to allow me to pull through.”"},{"id":"nance-mockridge","name":"Nance Mockridge","aliases":["Nance"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: “There’s a chance even for thee after this, Nance Mockridge.”"},{"id":"miss-newson","name":"Miss Newson","role":"minor","group":"g-newson","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “Now Susan, I want to have her called Miss Henchard—not Miss Newson.”"},{"id":"mrs-farfrae","name":"Mrs. Farfrae","role":"minor","group":"g-farfrae","firstAppearance":"s34","summary":"First mention: ““And I wished not to alarm Mrs.”"},{"id":"buzzford","name":"Buzzford","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s6","summary":"First mention: “Inside these illuminated holes, at a distance of about three inches, were ranged at this hour, as every passer knew, the ruddy polls of Billy Wills the glazier, Smart the shoemaker, Buzzford the general dealer, and ot…”"},{"id":"mrs-newson","name":"Mrs. Newson","role":"minor","group":"g-newson","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““I am not so sure of that,” said Mrs.”"},{"id":"council","name":"Council","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “Henchard, the Mayor, at the end of the table, a facing ye; and that’s the Council men right and left....”"},{"id":"charl","name":"Charl","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s36","summary":"First mention: ““Dost mind how you could jerk a trout ashore with a bramble, and not ruffle the stream, Charl?”"},{"id":"susan-henchard","name":"Susan Henchard","role":"minor","group":"g-henchard","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “A glance was sufficient to 